# A group/other-readable API key must be ROTATED, not chmod-repaired (banshee-czn,
# banshee-4d0). The previous implementation detected the loose mode and fixed it,
# leaving the daemon serving the key every local user could already read — the
# appearance of a trust boundary rather than the boundary. The test this pins
# previously asserted the OPPOSITE and passed, which is how the weakness survived
# having a test.
file: rust/banshee-api/src/auth.rs
test: an_overpermissive_key_is_rotated_not_merely_repaired
---OLD---
    let distrust = if mode & 0o077 != 0 {
        Some(KeyDistrust::Permissive(mode))
---NEW---
    let distrust = if false {
        Some(KeyDistrust::Permissive(mode))
